Subject: [PATCH] basic.cl: no [] subscripts on float4 in colorin_rgb

Reason (brief P4e): `v[i]` on an OpenCL vector is a Clang extension, not OpenCL C.
The Adreno OpenCL compiler (Adreno 650, compiler E031.37.12.07) refuses it with
"Attempt to use subscript to obtain element of 'float4'", basic.cl fails to build
and darktable drops the GPU at the first kernel file that fails.

tools/check-vector-subscripts.py finds exactly three such places in all of
data/kernels/*.cl at darktable 04477d32, all in colorin_rgb (basic.cl:1643, 1649).
Fix: write the matrix product with .x/.y/.z (constant index) and copy the clamped
vector into a private float[3] for the loop index. Each component is summed in the
same order (i = 0, 1, 2) as before, so the result is the same; .w stays 0.

Upstream: worth sending to darktable as is (see docs/experiments/P4e-adreno-kernels-REPORT.md).
Applied by: .github/workflows/apk-only.yml onto share/darktable/kernels of the engine archive
(patch -p3 from the kernel folder; from the darktable root use patch -p1 / git apply).
---
diff --git a/data/kernels/basic.cl b/data/kernels/basic.cl
index 5653ec2..24be601 100644
--- a/data/kernels/basic.cl
+++ b/data/kernels/basic.cl
@@ -1638,15 +1638,25 @@ colorin_rgb (read_only image2d_t in, write_only image2d_t out, const int width,
   }
 
   // the first matrix maps directly to working RGB, or to the clipping gamut
+  // OpenCL C has no [] on vectors (a Clang extension some drivers refuse): use components
   float4 linear = (float4)(0.0f);
-  for(int j = 0; j < 3; j++)
-    for(int i = 0; i < 3; i++) linear[j] += cmat[3*j+i] * cam[i];
+  for(int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
+  {
+    linear.x += cmat[i] * cam[i];
+    linear.y += cmat[3+i] * cam[i];
+    linear.z += cmat[6+i] * cam[i];
+  }
   if(clipping)
   {
-    float4 clipped = clamp(linear, 0.0f, 1.0f);
+    const float4 c4 = clamp(linear, 0.0f, 1.0f);
+    const float clipped[3] = { c4.x, c4.y, c4.z };
     linear = (float4)(0.0f);
-    for(int j = 0; j < 3; j++)
-      for(int i = 0; i < 3; i++) linear[j] += lmat[3*j+i] * clipped[i];
+    for(int i = 0; i < 3; i++)
+    {
+      linear.x += lmat[i] * clipped[i];
+      linear.y += lmat[3+i] * clipped[i];
+      linear.z += lmat[6+i] * clipped[i];
+    }
   }
   pixel = linear;
   if(use_hsm)
